datixxia™ groups awards by sector, location and period, so you can compare where commitments are growing and where they are slowing down.

The result is not a promise about the future. It is evidence about what has already been decided — so a supplier can see demand forming, and a planner can see which assumptions the data supports.
{% /split %}

{% takeaway
   text="Public contracts are the earliest honest record of where money will be spent. Reading them is not predicting the future — it is reading what has already been decided." /%}

If your plans depend on demand that has not arrived yet, this record is worth reading.
